[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243782942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3243782942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3243782942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BWDMe","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T04:59:05Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T04:59:05Z","body":"It is crossing to other screen, and it is exactly how it is supposed to work. `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` exist for a one single purpose, to ensure multiple native windows can be displayed on top of the main full-screen window (e.g, for the Godot editor), and it is deliberately breaking all kind of optimizations.\n\nIt this is not something you need, use `WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN` for any other purpose, it is normal fullscreen (naming is bad, modes should be `WINDOW_MODE_MULTIWINDOW_FULLSCREEN` and `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` or something like this).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243782942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244685791","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3244685791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3244685791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BZfnf","user":{"login":"SkanerSoft","id":13809475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODA5NDc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13809475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft","html_url":"https://github.com/SkanerSoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T10:11:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T10:11:47Z","body":"> WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN\n\nIt's because of the name that I've never used this mode. Damn it))","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244685791/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245090353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3245090353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3245090353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BbCYx","user":{"login":"PsiGreenEx","id":67715237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzE1MjM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67715237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx","html_url":"https://github.com/PsiGreenEx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T12:20:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T12:20:34Z","body":"> It is crossing to other screen, and it is exactly how it is supposed to work.\n\nIf that were the case, then why would it only be crossing over on the right side of the monitor? And why is this not a feature of 4.4.1.stable?\n\n> It this is not something you need, use `WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN` for any other purpose\n\nAnd that is what I will be using, though this is problem I have never experienced in a single other game. Godot specifically doesn't have alt-tab and window switching issues with exclusive fullscreen, but most games do, which is why in my experience, people with multi monitor setups default to using borderless.\n\n> (naming is bad, modes should be `WINDOW_MODE_MULTIWINDOW_FULLSCREEN` and `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` or something like this).\n\nOr at the very least `WINDOW_MODE_BORDERLESS_FULLSCREEN` and `WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN` for clarity.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245090353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245116493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3245116493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3245116493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BbIxN","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T12:28:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T12:30:54Z","body":"> If that were the case, then why would it only be crossing over on the right side of the monitor? And why is this not a feature of 4.4.1.stable?\n\nIn 4.5 it has an invisible border extending outside (specifically 2 px to the right, it's an arbitrary choice). In 4.4.1 there's visible 1 px border inside the window (in all directions), both added for the same purpose.\n\n> Or at the very least WINDOW_MODE_BORDERLESS_FULLSCREEN and WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN for clarity.\n\nNeither would be precise:\n\n- `WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN` is a borderless window with the size of the screen, this allows the GPU driver to disable composition (not render other windows), but not forcing or asking it to do so directly (in most cases it won't).\n- `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` is a borderless window that is not matching the size of the screen (by adding a border), to ensure no full-screen optimizations can be applied to it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245116493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245134480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3245134480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3245134480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BbNKQ","user":{"login":"PsiGreenEx","id":67715237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzE1MjM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67715237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx","html_url":"https://github.com/PsiGreenEx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T12:33:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T12:33:48Z","body":"Then what are the use-cases of \"borderless\" if the only difference is that it isn't technically even on one screen and it disables the optimizations meant for fullscreen? /genuine","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245134480/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245158520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3245158520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3245158520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BbTB4","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T12:40:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T12:40:40Z","body":"Editor (and other non-game UI), since it's using multiple windows, it will break if driver will decide to disable composition (which depends on user configuration). It's the same condition as messy alt-tab, but it case of editor it will make it completely unusable.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245158520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245190069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3245190069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3245190069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bbau1","user":{"login":"PsiGreenEx","id":67715237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzE1MjM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67715237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx","html_url":"https://github.com/PsiGreenEx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PsiGreenEx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T12:49:06Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T12:49:06Z","body":"Ah, I see. I'll let someone else close this issue if they determine that this is behavior is ideal, even if expected. Being 1 of like 7 people who have the combo of high refresh rate monitor and normal refresh rate monitor (using Windows, as terrible as it is) has caused some unique headaches for all sorts reasons, and I suspect this was never a problem anticipated when making the arbitrary descision of adding 2px to the right.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3245190069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3247060984","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3247060984","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3247060984,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bijf4","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T23:02:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T23:02:28Z","body":"For reference, this change was introduced in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/88852. It's generally welcomed by users as it removes the visible border and ensures integer-scaled games scale the same way as they'd do in exclusive fullscreen.\n\nHowever, for multi-monitor setups, this causes V-Sync to use the slowest monitor as a basis, since the window is technically spanning multiple monitors. This is a problem for non-game applications too, as it makes their update look choppy and less responsive. I wouldn't make the behavior differ depending on whether we're on a multi-monitor setup with differing refresh rates though, as that would lead to complicated troubleshooting. Your best workaround is probably to turn off V-Sync for now, and cap the framerate using `Engine.max_fps` to the fastest monitor's refresh rate.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3247060984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3249090979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3249090979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3249090979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BqTGj","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T12:41:35Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T12:41:35Z","body":"> However, for multi-monitor setups, this causes V-Sync to use the slowest monitor as a basis, since the window is technically spanning multiple monitors. This is a problem for non-game applications too, as it makes their update look choppy and less responsive. I wouldn't make the behavior differ depending on whether we're on a multi-monitor setup with differing refresh rates though, as that would lead to complicated troubleshooting. Your best workaround is probably to turn off V-Sync for now, and cap the framerate using Engine.max_fps to the fastest monitor's refresh rate.\n\nNot sure what can be done, moving all renderers to DXGI might give more control. But until it is done, it might be better to change it to extend down instead of right, since it much less likely there's a display under the main one.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3249090979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255546950","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3255546950","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3255546950,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CC7RG","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T20:35:14Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T20:35:14Z","body":"> It is crossing to other screen, and it is exactly how it is supposed to work. `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` exist for a one single purpose, to ensure multiple native windows can be displayed on top of the main full-screen window (e.g, for the Godot editor), and it is deliberately breaking all kind of optimizations.\n> \n> It this is not something you need, use `WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN` for any other purpose, it is normal fullscreen (naming is bad, modes should be `WINDOW_MODE_MULTIWINDOW_FULLSCREEN` and `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` or something like this).\n\nSee also: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11735\n\n> Then what are the use-cases of \"borderless\" if the only difference is that it isn't technically even on one screen and it disables the optimizations meant for fullscreen? /genuine\n\nSome configurations have buggy drivers where fullscreen optimizations cause problems. Ideally though, people should only be disabling/thwarting fullscreen optimizations if they need to, as doing so will also break tearing, VRR, HDR, and make framepacing worse.\n\n> Not sure what can be done, moving all renderers to DXGI might give more control. But until it is done, it might be better to change it to extend down instead of right, since it much less likely there's a display under the main one.\n\nWould it make sense to detect the user's monitor arrangement and then try to extend the window where there's no display? I.e. if the neighboring displays are to the left and right, extend off the bottom, but if the system is using dual monitors stacked vertically, extend off the side. I think this would only fail if you somehow have neighboring displays on all four sides, which would need five monitors, or some other exotic configuration.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255546950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255606472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3255606472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3255606472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CDJzI","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T20:48:52Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T20:53:03Z","body":"> Would it make sense to detect the user's monitor arrangement and then try to extend the window where there's no display? I.e. if the neighboring displays are to the left and right, extend off the bottom, but if the system is using dual monitors stacked vertically, extend off the side.\n\nExtending up or left will require some changes to the renderer to shift the displayed area. But down/right checks probably sufficient in most cases. It's also possible to check refresh rate of the displays before choosing.\n\nSomething like:\n- if no display under, expand down\n- elif no display on the right, expand right\n- else select direction with min rate difference","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255606472/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258892556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3258892556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3258892556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CPsEM","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T16:04:23Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T16:04:43Z","body":"That'll cause problems for specific 3-monitor setups, but it'd still be an improvement over the current situation. I think this makes sense for a quick fix for more common setups. We can reevaluate extending up/left later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258892556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714512657","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110179#issuecomment-3714512657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110179","id":3714512657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dZvcR","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/use